            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="COA01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Robert/Romeo</forename>
                        <surname>Coates</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1772">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1848"/>
                    <occupation>Amateur actor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Orig from Antigua; was at school in Britain. Appeared on stage 1810-16;
                            booed off and withdrew for a period. Godwin meets him initially at the
                            theatre or in theatrical company but is then calling on him - as befits
                            his relationship with a very wealthy man who seems keen to spend a
                            fortune. Coates is not in the diary between 1814 and 1822. His DNB entry
                            suggests he squandered a large part of his considerable fortune but he
                            eventually married Emma Anne Robinson in 1823 (plausibly returning to the UK the
                            previous year).</p>
                    </note>
